  "_comment": "Negative. Two machine-adjudication proofs are independent on all five axes (distinct issuers, independence groups, providers, model IDs, and response artifacts) but carry DIFFERENT rkaf:sealedRequestDigest values -- they answered two different sealed questions, not the same one twice. Two machines answering two questions is not a corroboration of one; caught by rkaf:MachineAdjudicationIndependentPairShape. See the companion positive fixture for the case this complements: three machines answering the SAME sealed question is valid (spec/rkaf-analysis.md 3.4, 4 extension; spec/rkaf-refspec.md corrected 2026-08-09) -- independence and sameness of question are separate, both-required conditions, and this fixture isolates the second one failing."
